/T (Defect 2 \(does not compile\): p is a pointer \(struct account *p = list\), but the program uses p.number and p.balance. The dot operator works only on a structure variable. For a pointer the arrow operator is needed \(p->number, p- >balance\). The compiler reported: "'p' is a pointer; did you mean to use '->'?")
/E (Defect 2 \(does not compile\): p is a pointer \(struct account *p = list\), but the program uses p.number and p.balance. The dot operator works only on a structure variable. For a pointer the arrow operator is needed \(p->number, p- >balance\). The compiler reported: "'p' is a pointer; did you mean to use '->'?")
