/T (auto variables arecreated when a block starts and destroyed when it ends. static local variables are created once and keep their value for the whole program, but are visible only in their function. A global variable is defined in one file and shared with other files by declaring it extern. A register variable is a request to keep a fast variable in a CPU register; its address cannot be taken.)
/E (auto variables arecreated when a block starts and destroyed when it ends. static local variables are created once and keep their value for the whole program, but are visible only in their function. A global variable is defined in one file and shared with other files by declaring it extern. A register variable is a request to keep a fast variable in a CPU register; its address cannot be taken.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [12]
